    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="1502" n="1478" xml:id="pg1478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2079: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the French
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi><anchor n="55" xml:id="d399-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        CFM(46)(NY)63</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-07"
                            >December 7, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Questions Relating to
                        Germany</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">draft agenda for the next session
                        of the council of foreign ministers</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1)</label>
                    <item>Future frontiers of Germany.</item>
                    <label>2)</label>
                    <item>Control measures for ensuring European security. <list>
                            <item>—United States Draft of Four Power Treaty.</item>
                            <item>—other measures for economic and military control.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>3)</label>
                    <item>Consideration of French proposals for the Ruhr and Rhineland in relation
                        to items 1 and 2.</item>
                    <label>4)</label>
                    <item>Consideration of a report to be obtained from Allied Control Authority in
                        Berlin dealing with: <list>
                            <item>—demilitarization of Germany,</item>
                            <item>—democratization and denazification,</item>
                            <item>—reparation,</item>
                            <item>—economic unity and central agencies as well as provisional
                                political organization of Germany under quadripartite
                                Government.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>5)</label>
                    <item>General outline of a permanent political organization for Germany.</item>
                    <label>6)</label>
                    <item>Consideration of a report from the Allied Control Authority in Berlin on
                        the liquidation of Prussia.</item>
                    <label>7)</label>
                    <item>Consideration of the report already submitted by the Committee of Coal
                        Experts.</item>
                    <label>8)</label>
                    <item>General outline of the Peace Treaty with Germany.</item>
                    <label>9)</label>
                    <item>Treaty with Austria and related matters.</item>
                    <label>10)</label>
                    <item>Limitation of European occupation forces.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d399-f1" n="55" type="source" xml:id="d399-f1-content">
                <p>This proposal was considered by the Council of Foreign Ministers at its 19th
                    Meeting, December 9, 1946; see the United States Delegation Minutes, <ref
                        target="#pg1481">p. 1481</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
